      <h1>Synthetic decision brief on forward pricing rate review window</h1>
      <div class="meta-row">
  <span>As of <time datetime="2026-02-01">2026-02-01</time></span>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  <span>Review by <time datetime="2026-07-31">2026-07-31</time></span>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  <span><b>0 of 2</b> claims supported</span>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  
  <span>Last verified <span class="unver">Never verified</span></span>
  
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  <span>Readiness <b>SYNTHETIC-NOW</b></span>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
  <span class="mono">est-rate-window-brief</span>
</div>
      <div class="page-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn sm" id="fb:copyLinkBtn" data-copy-link="est-rate-window-brief">Copy link</button>
        <div class="seg" id="fb:wordingSeg" role="group" aria-label="Wording">
          <button type="button" data-wording="both" aria-pressed="true">Both</button>
          <button type="button" data-wording="plain" aria-pressed="false">Plain</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="sheet">
      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="question">
        <h2 id="question">Question</h2>
        
        <p>Should the synthetic pricing team adopt the 10 days <span class="term" data-pv="term:rate_window" data-pv-title="rate window" data-pv-body="Synthetic period allowed to complete a forward pricing rate check.">rate window</span> for baseline updates <a class="cite-n" href="#cite-1" data-pv="cite:1" data-pv-title="CL-EST-0003" data-pv-body="Synthetic rate review window is 10 days under current guidance." aria-label="Source 1">1</a>?</p>

        
      </section>

      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="recommendation">
        <h2 id="recommendation">Recommendation</h2>
        
        <p>Adopt the synthetic 10 days rate window for all new synthetic <span class="term" data-pv="term:cost_baseline" data-pv-title="cost baseline" data-pv-body="Synthetic time-phased budget basis used to measure synthetic estimating variance.">cost baseline</span> updates <a class="cite-n" href="#cite-2" data-pv="cite:2" data-pv-title="CL-EST-0003" data-pv-body="Synthetic rate review window is 10 days under current guidance." aria-label="Source 2">2</a>.</p>

        
      </section>

      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="evidence">
        <h2 id="evidence">Evidence</h2>
        
        <ul>
<li>Current synthetic pricing guidance sets a 10 days window <a class="cite-n" href="#cite-3" data-pv="cite:3" data-pv-title="CL-EST-0003" data-pv-body="Synthetic rate review window is 10 days under current guidance." aria-label="Source 3">3</a>.</li>
<li>Synthetic escalation placeholder stands at 3 percent per year <a class="cite-n" href="#cite-4" data-pv="cite:4" data-pv-title="CL-EST-0001" data-pv-body="Synthetic escalation placeholder is 3 percent per year for fixture examples." aria-label="Source 4">4</a>.</li>
</ul>

        
      </section>

      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="options">
        <h2 id="options">Options</h2>
        
        <ul>
<li>Adopt the 10 days synthetic window immediately <a class="cite-n" href="#cite-5" data-pv="cite:5" data-pv-title="CL-EST-0003" data-pv-body="Synthetic rate review window is 10 days under current guidance." aria-label="Source 5">5</a>.</li>
<li>Retain manual case-by-case scheduling until onboarding completes.</li>
</ul>

        
      </section>

      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="unknowns">
        <h2 id="unknowns">Unknowns</h2>
        
        <ul>
<li>Multi-year synthetic escalation index selection remains open <span class="cite neutral" data-pv="q:Q-002" data-pv-title="Q-002" data-pv-body="Which synthetic escalation index applies to multi-year pricing workbooks?">Q-002</span>.</li>
</ul>

        
      </section>

      <section class="part" aria-labelledby="next-action">
        <h2 id="next-action">Next action</h2>
        
        <p>The Estimating Lead will revisit this synthetic decision when the escalation index question closes.</p>

        
      </section>

